-- title:
--   Original ruin-stopped source grid convergence and eventual Stieltjes domination prove the complete HJB dividend expectation bound
-- statement:
--   The strongest source-faithful finite-horizon original dividend verification bridge: for original X and D, genuine source/discount stopped triangular grid convergence to M+G and only eventual one-sided domination of the complementary complete Stieltjes dividend grid by H suffice for the stopped Itô-Meyer upper estimate. With source HJB generator and gradient inequalities, q>0, w(0)>=0, BV C1 or UBV C2 and original right-continuous ruin-stopped clock, and with a.e. measurable terminal/cash plus integrable centred M and nonpositive integrable G+H, the full expected terminal-plus-cash and complete discounted dividend bounds follow. No exact dividend-grid limit or independent cash/terminal integrability is assumed. The physical source martingale limit and one-sided dividend domination remain owner hypotheses.
-- source:
--   Avram Prop 4(i), Eq (5.11)-(5.13), composition of accepted one-sided original grid-to-Ito upper interface de45bfb6 (once Proved) and accepted measurable-data one-sided HJB budget 8cd5e123.

